 "summary": "After the engine fire the aircraft must land soon, above its maximum landing weight. This is permitted only with the QRH OVERWEIGHT LANDING procedure. Plan a long, early-stabilised approach and use flaps FULL unless performance limits it. Turn the packs OFF (or supply them from the APU) for go-around thrust. Cross the threshold at VLS and touch down below 360 ft/min, then use max reverse early.",
